    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Improve memory locality and loop order by using a blocked approach to process submatrices in larger chunks, ensuring correct boundary handling.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\"Reorganize the matrix processing into blocks\", \"Adjust loop order for better cache performance\"],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n\\nint main() {\\n\\tint n, s;\\n\\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\\n\\tstd::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n\\tfor(int i=0; i<n; i++)\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0; j<n; j++) \\n\\t\\t\\tscanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n\\tassert(s < n);\\n\\tassert(n < 8000);\\n\\tassert(s > 0);\\n\\tassert(n > 0);\\n\\n\\tconst int blockSize = 32; // Define a block size for better cache performance\\n\\tint mxSum = INT_MIN;\\n\\n\\tfor(int bi = 0; bi < n; bi += blockSize) {\\n\\t\\tfor(int bj = 0; bj < n; bj += blockSize) {\\n\\t\\t\\tint sum = 0;\\n\\t\\t\\t// Initialize the first block\\n\\t\\t\\tfor(int i = bi; i < std::min(bi + blockSize, n); i++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor(int j = bj; j < std::min(bj + blockSize, n); j++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif(i < s && j < s) sum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Slide the block horizontally and vertically\\n\\t\\t\\tfor(int i = bi; i + s <= n; i++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tint enteringRow = i + s - 1;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif(enteringRow >= n) break;\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor(int j = bj; j < n; j += blockSize) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tint blockEndJ = std::min(j + blockSize, n);\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t// Slide the block horizontally within the row\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif(j > 0) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tfor(int k = i; k < enteringRow; k++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum -= matrix[k][j-1];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif(blockEndJ < n) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tfor(int k = i; k < enteringRow; k++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[k][blockEndJ];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t// Slide the block vertically within the column\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif(i > bi) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tfor(int k = j; k < blockEndJ; k++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum -= matrix[i-1][k];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif(enteringRow < n) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tfor(int k = j; k < blockEndJ; k++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[enteringRow][k];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tprintf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"Reorganized the matrix processing into blocks of size 32 to improve memory locality and cache performance. Adjusted loop order to ensure correct boundary handling while sliding submatrices.\"\n}"
